course: dictionary
lesson: 9738
title: Sunscreen and staying safe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sunscreen is a cream or spray you put on your skin to protect it from the Sun's harmful rays. Context gives you clues: «Sunscreen should be at least SPF 30» and must be put on again every two hours. Those clues show it is something you put on your skin before going out in strong sun.
explain: «A girl in Queensland spent a whole day at the beach without sunscreen or a hat; her skin blistered.» The word without tells you what was missing, and the blisters show the harm. So sunscreen is the thing that protects skin from that harm. Try the swap check: put "a cream that protects your skin from the Sun" in place of sunscreen, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Sunscreen has other names. In the UK it is often called sun cream, and sunblock means the same thing. In Australia and New Zealand, people learn «Slip, slop, slap»: slip on a shirt, slop on sunscreen, slap on a hat. Sunscreen works best with shade, a hat and sunglasses, not on its own.
fact: Sunscreen is a cream or spray that protects your skin from the Sun's harmful rays.
fact: Sun cream and sunblock are other names for sunscreen.
fact: «SPF» is the number that shows how strongly sunscreen protects, and «SPF 30» is the lowest strength the example recommends.
fact: Put sunscreen on about 20 minutes before going out in strong sun, then put more on every two hours and after swimming.
fact: «Ultraviolet rays» in sunlight can cause sunburn, even on a cloudy day, because most of them pass through thin cloud.
exercise: «Sunscreen should be at least SPF 30 and be put on again every two hours.» What is sunscreen? | A pool you swim in | *A cream or spray that protects your skin from the Sun | Hot drink with milk | A hat with a wide brim
exercise: «Sunscreen should be at least SPF 30 and be put on again every two hours and after swimming.» When should you put sunscreen on again? | *Every two hours and after swimming | Never, once it is on | Only once a day, in the morning | Only when it is cloudy
exercise: In the UK, sunscreen is often called another name. What is it? | Sunshine | Sunflower | *Sun cream | Sun hat
test: What does sunscreen help to prevent? | Hunger | Wet feet | *Sunburn | Tiredness
test: In «Slip, slop, slap», what does slop mean? | Put on a hat | Go swimming | Put on a shirt | *Put on sunscreen
exam: «Sunscreen works best with shade, a hat and sunglasses.» What works best alongside sunscreen? | Running fast in the sun | Ice cream | *Shade, a hat and sunglasses | Deep water
